urrent physical distancing to  deepen our separation from each other  and increase our loneliness which in  turn has long-term impacts on our  increased risk for heart disease  dementia depression and anxiety or we  can go in the opposite direction and say  that we are gonna use this moment to  reset our lives to recommit to making  relationships a priority in our lives  and there are some simple steps that we  can take to do that right now even  though we don't have the ability to see  each other in person and that's what I  really go through and it was it was an  instant I was inspired to do it really  by by folks who taught me that as a  doctor you know we we see lots of  illnesses like diabetes and hypertension  doctor more thing but this is one that  we have not been paying enough attention  to I think that's right dr. Morton I was  gonna mention to those tips in the book  one of them being take time every day 15  minutes to connect with the people most  important you in your life and second  when you do that make sure you focus  don't have another thing going on don't  be cooking at the same time just  one-on-one connection so important as  we're  mind ER right now dr. Vivek Murthy thank  you very much and your book togetherness  it goes on sale tomorrow and you can  hear more from dr. Murthy about the  fight against loneliness on today's CBS  this morning podcast it's available  wherever you like to get your podcasts
 

